+*   **Primitive Growth:** If a primitive grows outside its allocated texture grid (due to lack of allocation or hitting the 256 limit), zero-padding is used. Since texels are offsets, this reduces to the DC color [S1].
+*   **Sub-texel Details:** Limiting $t2pr \ge 2$ does not significantly degrade quality because sub-texel details are retrieved via alpha blending and primitive overlap [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
 
 **Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   **Memory:** The number of parameters is 59 per primitive plus 3 per texel. The total number of texels is dynamic. On DeepBlending, it uses 21.6M texels and 78.1M params [S1]. On Mip-Nerf-360, 46.6M texels and 152.6M params [S1]. On Tanks&Temples, 10.4M texels and 41.1M params [S1].
-*   **Training Time:** Training is 1.5-2x slower than 2DGS due to per-ray texture querying overhead [S1].
-*   **Rendering Time:** Rendering is 25% slower than 2DGS [S1].
